1
00:00:09,588 --> 00:00:12,420
A fish swims, and the water has no end.

2
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,509
Must it reach the end of the
water, to know the water?

3
00:00:16,312 --> 00:00:18,940
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:22,898
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

5
00:00:23,708 --> 00:00:28,587
In Part 7, the shore and the boat
took away the seat outside the event,

6
00:00:28,667 --> 00:00:30,127
and the doer behind it.

7
00:00:30,207 --> 00:00:35,901
In Part 8, firewood and ash took away a
past or a future, needed to complete it.

8
00:00:35,981 --> 00:00:41,010
One more way something could stand
outside the event remains. A wider place.

9
00:00:41,090 --> 00:00:45,073
Here is only a small part of the
world, and the rest lies further on.

10
00:00:45,153 --> 00:00:48,596
Surely the event is complete
only when the rest is added.

11
00:00:49,392 --> 00:00:52,496
Dōgen's image for this
is the fish and the bird.

12
00:00:52,576 --> 00:00:56,495
And then, in this part, I
bring the four images together.

13
00:00:57,292 --> 00:00:59,716
First, the fish and the bird.

14
00:01:00,536 --> 00:01:03,635
Near the end of the
Genjōkōan, Dōgen writes:

15
00:01:03,715 --> 00:01:08,531
a fish swims in the water, and however
far it swims, the water has no end.

16
00:01:08,611 --> 00:01:13,653
A bird flies in the sky, and however
far it flies, the sky has no end.

17
00:01:13,733 --> 00:01:16,049
Yet neither has ever left its element.

18
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:19,515
When the need is large, the use is large.

19
00:01:19,595 --> 00:01:21,893
When it is small, the use is small.

20
00:01:21,973 --> 00:01:24,461
Each covers its whole range completely.

21
00:01:24,541 --> 00:01:27,124
A bird that left the
sky would die at once.

22
00:01:27,204 --> 00:01:29,515
And so would a fish that left the water.

23
00:01:29,595 --> 00:01:32,278
Water is life, and sky is life.

24
00:01:33,088 --> 00:01:37,641
A fish or a bird that tried to reach the
end of the water or the sky before moving

25
00:01:37,721 --> 00:01:40,404
in it would find no way, and no place.

26
00:01:40,484 --> 00:01:43,750
When you find your place
right here, practice happens.

27
00:01:44,564 --> 00:01:48,438
Just before this, Dōgen notes
that from a boat far out at sea,

28
00:01:48,518 --> 00:01:51,499
with no land in sight,
the ocean looks round.

29
00:01:51,579 --> 00:01:53,714
But it is neither round nor square.

30
00:01:53,794 --> 00:01:55,684
To a fish it is a palace.

31
00:01:55,764 --> 00:01:58,578
To a heavenly being, a string of jewels.

32
00:01:58,658 --> 00:02:01,667
It looks round only as
far as the eye can reach.

33
00:02:02,472 --> 00:02:04,176
How is this usually read?

34
00:02:04,256 --> 00:02:06,214
It is a teaching on practice.

35
00:02:06,294 --> 00:02:08,619
You do not need to understand everything,

36
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:11,703
or reach the end of the
water, before you begin.

37
00:02:11,783 --> 00:02:15,032
Practise where you are, and
the Way is realised there.

38
00:02:15,112 --> 00:02:19,557
The water and the sky are often read
as the Way, or as buddha nature.

39
00:02:19,637 --> 00:02:23,284
And the fish and the bird as the
practitioner who lives in it.

40
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,478
Here is how I see it.

41
00:02:26,672 --> 00:02:29,925
The habit sees a fish
inside a container of water.

42
00:02:30,005 --> 00:02:32,289
And a bird inside a box of sky.

43
00:02:32,369 --> 00:02:34,422
It wants to know where the edges are.

44
00:02:34,502 --> 00:02:37,443
And it thinks it must reach
them, to know the whole.

45
00:02:38,244 --> 00:02:41,823
Anatta takes away the seeker who
stands apart from the swimming.

46
00:02:41,903 --> 00:02:43,404
There is just the swimming.

47
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,570
And dependent arising shows the rest.

48
00:02:46,650 --> 00:02:49,328
The fish is a fish only with the water.

49
00:02:49,408 --> 00:02:52,616
And the water is life for the
fish only in the swimming.

50
00:02:52,696 --> 00:02:54,546
They are designated together.

51
00:02:54,626 --> 00:02:57,603
Wherever the fish is,
the swimming is complete.

52
00:02:57,683 --> 00:03:00,687
It does not need the whole
ocean added up to be whole.

53
00:03:00,767 --> 00:03:04,115
Large or small, it covers
its range completely.

54
00:03:04,916 --> 00:03:08,074
And Dōgen himself guards
against the big reading.

55
00:03:08,154 --> 00:03:11,539
The ocean looks round only
as far as the eye can reach.

56
00:03:11,619 --> 00:03:13,862
No one ever meets the whole as a sum.

57
00:03:13,942 --> 00:03:15,642
So completeness is here.

58
00:03:15,722 --> 00:03:18,228
Not in a grand total, somewhere else.

59
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:22,149
That is the taste of
this image. No elsewhere.

60
00:03:22,229 --> 00:03:23,793
Being at home where I am.

61
00:03:23,873 --> 00:03:26,660
There is nowhere further to
go to find what is missing,

62
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:28,485
because nothing is missing.

63
00:03:29,284 --> 00:03:32,016
And the conditions are
not outside influences,

64
00:03:32,097 --> 00:03:33,665
pressing in from beyond.

65
00:03:33,745 --> 00:03:36,912
The water does not surround
the fish as a foreign thing.

66
00:03:36,992 --> 00:03:38,706
It takes part as the swimming.

67
00:03:38,786 --> 00:03:40,893
The air does not surround the sound.

68
00:03:40,973 --> 00:03:42,714
It takes part as the sounding.

69
00:03:42,794 --> 00:03:45,857
This is what I call the
end of external conditions.

70
00:03:46,664 --> 00:03:50,067
And where I part. I keep
the reading on practice.

71
00:03:50,147 --> 00:03:54,808
But I do not make the water a ground, such
as buddha nature as a vast medium the fish

72
00:03:54,888 --> 00:04:00,112
swims in. The water is as dependent
as the fish. Neither is the floor.

73
00:04:00,924 --> 00:04:02,628
Second, the fan.

74
00:04:03,496 --> 00:04:05,744
The Genjōkōan ends with a story.

75
00:04:05,824 --> 00:04:08,121
A Chan master was fanning himself.

76
00:04:08,201 --> 00:04:11,355
A monk asked: the nature
of wind is permanent,

77
00:04:11,435 --> 00:04:13,746
and there is no place it does not reach.

78
00:04:13,826 --> 00:04:15,925
Why, then, do you use a fan?

79
00:04:16,724 --> 00:04:20,942
The master said: you know only that
the nature of wind is permanent.

80
00:04:21,022 --> 00:04:24,080
You do not yet know the meaning
of its reaching everywhere.

81
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,200
The monk asked what that meaning was.

82
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:29,492
The master just went on
fanning. And the monk bowed.

83
00:04:30,288 --> 00:04:34,828
Dōgen comments: if you say that because
the wind is everywhere there is no need to

84
00:04:34,908 --> 00:04:38,759
fan, you know neither permanence,
nor the nature of wind.

85
00:04:39,556 --> 00:04:41,260
How is this usually read?

86
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:45,581
Buddha nature is everywhere, yet
it must be realised in practice.

87
00:04:45,661 --> 00:04:48,425
Practice and realisation are not two.

88
00:04:49,232 --> 00:04:50,529
Here is how I see it.

89
00:04:50,609 --> 00:04:54,496
The monk's mistake is the one this
whole section has been taking apart.

90
00:04:54,576 --> 00:04:58,545
He takes the nature of wind as
something already there, everywhere.

91
00:04:58,625 --> 00:05:01,398
A given, waiting, needing nothing.

92
00:05:01,478 --> 00:05:03,658
Then the fanning seems pointless.

93
00:05:04,452 --> 00:05:07,909
But there is no wind waiting
everywhere, behind the fanning.

94
00:05:07,989 --> 00:05:09,553
The wind is this fanning.

95
00:05:09,633 --> 00:05:13,425
The hand, the fan, the
air, the cool on the face,

96
00:05:13,505 --> 00:05:15,151
all at once, complete.

97
00:05:15,231 --> 00:05:19,159
Reaching everywhere does not mean a
substance spread through all places.

98
00:05:19,239 --> 00:05:22,637
It means that wherever it is
realised, it is wholly there.

99
00:05:22,717 --> 00:05:25,042
As the fish's swimming is wholly there.

100
00:05:25,122 --> 00:05:28,335
The master does not explain. He fans.

101
00:05:29,152 --> 00:05:31,291
Now the four images, together.

102
00:05:32,108 --> 00:05:36,294
Each image takes away one way that
something could stand outside the event,

103
00:05:36,374 --> 00:05:37,574
and complete it.

104
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:40,732
The shore takes away a seer outside.

105
00:05:40,812 --> 00:05:43,725
What is left is one
moving, owned by no one.

106
00:05:44,524 --> 00:05:46,948
The boat takes away a doer behind.

107
00:05:47,028 --> 00:05:50,485
What is left is the act, its
conditions wholly at work.

108
00:05:51,296 --> 00:05:55,188
Firewood and ash take away a
past or a future to complete it.

109
00:05:55,268 --> 00:05:57,747
What is left is this position, complete.

110
00:05:58,548 --> 00:06:02,154
The fish and the bird take away
a wider place to complete it.

111
00:06:02,234 --> 00:06:05,134
What is left is here,
the whole range covered.

112
00:06:05,944 --> 00:06:08,871
Take away all four, and
the event lacks nothing.

113
00:06:08,951 --> 00:06:12,191
No wider whole stands
behind it, to complete it.

114
00:06:13,004 --> 00:06:15,619
And each image is complete
as its dependence.

115
00:06:15,699 --> 00:06:18,689
The moving arises between boat and shore.

116
00:06:18,769 --> 00:06:20,782
Rower and boat make each other.

117
00:06:20,862 --> 00:06:22,412
The ash comes from the wood.

118
00:06:22,492 --> 00:06:24,396
The fish lives by the water.

119
00:06:24,476 --> 00:06:27,534
That is why total exertion
is not a row of islands,

120
00:06:27,614 --> 00:06:31,366
each sealed in its own
completeness. Each event is whole.

121
00:06:31,446 --> 00:06:34,971
And its wholeness is its
conditions, fully spent as it.

122
00:06:35,784 --> 00:06:38,249
Some other tastes run through all four.

123
00:06:39,052 --> 00:06:40,974
Seamless, without fusion.

124
00:06:41,054 --> 00:06:43,039
Boundaries lose their solidity.

125
00:06:43,119 --> 00:06:45,349
Yet distinctions never disappear.

126
00:06:45,429 --> 00:06:47,196
Sound never becomes colour.

127
00:06:47,276 --> 00:06:49,398
The shore never becomes the boat.

128
00:06:49,478 --> 00:06:52,101
Difference is, if anything, more vivid.

129
00:06:52,181 --> 00:06:54,361
But the invisible walls are gone.

130
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:57,761
Activity, without things behind it.

131
00:06:57,841 --> 00:07:03,250
Nouns turn into verbs. Rowing.
Burning. Swimming. Fanning.

132
00:07:03,330 --> 00:07:04,867
And a trap waits here.

133
00:07:04,947 --> 00:07:08,237
The mind wants some subtle
medium underneath the verbs.

134
00:07:08,317 --> 00:07:13,332
Awareness, or energy, or a universal
process, flowing through everything.

135
00:07:13,412 --> 00:07:16,144
That is the substrate again, only liquid.

136
00:07:16,224 --> 00:07:18,893
The activity has nothing flowing under it.

137
00:07:19,692 --> 00:07:22,972
Luminous. None of this
is merely functional.

138
00:07:23,052 --> 00:07:24,589
It is vivid and clear.

139
00:07:24,669 --> 00:07:28,316
The clarity is the event
appearing, not a light added to it.

140
00:07:29,128 --> 00:07:30,995
Light, and trustworthy.

141
00:07:31,075 --> 00:07:34,936
Because nothing stands on its own,
nothing has to hold itself up.

142
00:07:35,016 --> 00:07:38,849
And without any essence,
things still work, reliably.

143
00:07:38,929 --> 00:07:42,358
The world holds together,
without anything holding it.

144
00:07:43,172 --> 00:07:45,447
What total exertion does not mean.

145
00:07:46,248 --> 00:07:48,917
It is very easily heard in a bigger way.

146
00:07:48,997 --> 00:07:51,607
The whole cosmos is
present in each moment.

147
00:07:51,687 --> 00:07:54,134
The entire universe rings in this bell.

148
00:07:54,214 --> 00:07:55,751
That sounds profound.

149
00:07:55,831 --> 00:07:58,034
But it quietly brings back a ground.

150
00:07:58,114 --> 00:08:01,231
If a cosmic Whole is
packed inside each moment,

151
00:08:01,347 --> 00:08:03,903
or stands behind it as what it really is,

152
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:08,890
then the Whole has become the floor,
instead of the parts. That is holism.

153
00:08:08,970 --> 00:08:10,955
It changes which comes first.

154
00:08:11,035 --> 00:08:13,133
But it does not remove the floor.

155
00:08:13,948 --> 00:08:18,587
So, to gather the guards. Not
one Whole. Not one substance.

156
00:08:18,667 --> 00:08:21,889
No cosmos packed inside. Not islands.

157
00:08:21,969 --> 00:08:25,231
Not a line, or a web. Not a medium.

158
00:08:25,311 --> 00:08:27,908
And not the parts as
the real stuff either.

159
00:08:27,988 --> 00:08:31,458
Neither the whole nor the parts
are found standing on their own.

160
00:08:32,264 --> 00:08:36,618
The rower stays a rower. The
boat a boat. The sky the sky.

161
00:08:36,698 --> 00:08:38,764
Nothing has merged into one thing.

162
00:08:38,844 --> 00:08:43,253
There is just this stroke of the oar,
fully exerted. And then the next.

163
00:08:44,052 --> 00:08:46,612
A taste that cannot yet explain itself.

164
00:08:47,416 --> 00:08:49,378
Total exertion perplexed me.

165
00:08:49,458 --> 00:08:51,933
Because it was complete
as lived experience,

166
00:08:52,013 --> 00:08:54,175
while its meaning stayed unresolved.

167
00:08:54,255 --> 00:08:58,115
I knew with certainty that the world did
not consist of independently existing

168
00:08:58,195 --> 00:09:00,737
things. Yet I could not say why.

169
00:09:00,817 --> 00:09:02,666
How can the rower be the rowing?

170
00:09:02,746 --> 00:09:05,044
How can nothing stand behind the event?

171
00:09:05,124 --> 00:09:07,956
Why does this not collapse
into one big Whole?

172
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:10,284
The taste had changed.

173
00:09:10,364 --> 00:09:12,050
The grammar of thought had not.

174
00:09:12,130 --> 00:09:14,468
This is not a failure of practice.

175
00:09:14,548 --> 00:09:16,293
It is how this matures.

176
00:09:17,088 --> 00:09:19,961
And the grammar did not
come from deeper absorption.

177
00:09:20,041 --> 00:09:24,594
It came from seeing that the old chariot
is not an analogy about a vehicle.

178
00:09:24,674 --> 00:09:30,069
It is an exact description of this very
moment. Not the wheels. Not the axle.

179
00:09:30,149 --> 00:09:33,520
Not apart from them. And yet
it carries its passenger.

180
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:38,018
The rowing, the boat and the river are
designated together in just that way.

181
00:09:38,098 --> 00:09:41,102
And so are the wood, the fire and the ash.

182
00:09:41,182 --> 00:09:43,308
And the fish, and the water.

183
00:09:44,116 --> 00:09:45,712
So, which holds?

184
00:09:46,688 --> 00:09:48,093
By experience.

185
00:09:48,173 --> 00:09:53,460
When I swim, or walk, or hear the bell, is
the event met as a small piece of a larger

186
00:09:53,540 --> 00:09:55,498
world, lying further on?

187
00:09:55,578 --> 00:09:58,963
Is a Whole met behind it,
or a cosmos met inside it?

188
00:09:59,043 --> 00:10:01,816
What is met is the
activity, here, complete.

189
00:10:01,896 --> 00:10:05,530
With its conditions coming through
as it, and nothing outside it.

190
00:10:06,324 --> 00:10:09,795
By logic. If the fish were
a fish apart from the water,

191
00:10:09,875 --> 00:10:11,860
it would not die when taken out.

192
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:15,664
If the event were complete only
when the whole world was added up,

193
00:10:15,744 --> 00:10:17,295
it would never be complete.

194
00:10:17,375 --> 00:10:20,057
Because no one ever
meets the whole as a sum.

195
00:10:20,872 --> 00:10:26,761
By working. Nothing works the less for
this. The fish swims. The bird flies.

196
00:10:26,841 --> 00:10:28,804
The fan cools the face.

197
00:10:29,612 --> 00:10:33,893
So separate things linked by conditions,
or one great Whole showing itself in

198
00:10:33,973 --> 00:10:36,248
parts, is not the truer view.

199
00:10:36,328 --> 00:10:40,247
Both are the default, carried
by habit, and by nouns.

200
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:43,641
None of this makes my
everyday words false.

201
00:10:43,721 --> 00:10:45,543
The fish swims in the sea.

202
00:10:45,623 --> 00:10:47,731
I fan myself on a hot day.

203
00:10:47,811 --> 00:10:51,277
What fails is only a fish, a sea, a wind,

204
00:10:51,357 --> 00:10:53,795
or a cosmos, standing on its own.

205
00:10:54,604 --> 00:10:58,713
This is Section 2, Part 9 of
the Dependent Arising series.

206
00:10:59,528 --> 00:11:04,398
In Part 10, I go to the classical home
of this taste, in Chinese Buddhism.

207
00:11:04,478 --> 00:11:06,422
Worlds in a grain of dust.

208
00:11:06,502 --> 00:11:09,058
A rafter, and the building it makes.

209
00:11:09,138 --> 00:11:12,432
And a net of jewels, each
reflecting all the others.

